<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[Hi&nbsp;<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">[NAME]</span>]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal">September is National Sickle Cell
Awareness Month, and <b><i><span style="background:white">Did you know that
many individuals who are Black are ideal blood donors for patients with sickle
cell disease</span></i></b><span style="background:white">?</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Because one of the primary
treatments for sickle cell disease is blood transfusion, we’re asking </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; background: white;">community partners such as yours, to join the Red
Cross&nbsp;and host a blood <span class="normaltextrun">drive in part </span></span><span class="normaltextrun" style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="background: white;">of <i>Joined by Blood</i>, a focused time period
within our Sickle Cell Initiative throughout the months of September and
October.<i>&nbsp;</i></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">By hosting a blood drive, you can help ensure that there
is an adequate supply of healthy blood available for those who need it most.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b style="font-size: 12pt;"><i>One in 3 African American blood
donors are a match for people with sickle cell disease</i></b><span style="font-size: 12pt;">. The Red Cross is continuously trying to recruit more
blood donors who are Black.&nbsp; We would be
honored to have your organization partner with us for this important cause.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b style="font-size: 12pt;"><i>By
hosting a blood drive</i></b><span style="font-size: 12pt;">, and promoting blood donation among African
Americans, you can help make a difference in the lives of individuals with
sickle cell disease and other patients who require blood transfusions.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">We would be happy to provide you
with more information and answer any questions you may have. You can also find
more information at </span><a href="https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/blood-types/diversity/african-american-blood-donors.html" style="font-size: 12pt;">RedCrossBlood.org/OurBlood</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;">.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b style="font-size: 12pt;"><i>September and October calendars are open and prime dates are
filing fast. Let’s talk and get your blood drive scheduled</i></b><b style="font-size: 12pt;">!</b><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp; Please call me at xxx-xxx-xxxx</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Thank you for considering joining us in supporting Sickle Cell
Awareness Month.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">









</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Sincerely,</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">[NAME]</span></p>]]></td>
</tr>
